"""Build B2 report from recorded descriptors and example figures."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def main():
    data=json.loads((ROOT/'measurements.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));records=data['records']
    rows=''.join(f'<tr><td><a href="#image-{r["image"][4:8]}">{r["image"][4:8]}</a></td><td>{r["input_points"]}</td><td>{r["valid_count"]}</td><td>{r["invalid_support"]+r["invalid_low_variance"]}</td><td>{r["std_min_in_bounds"]:.5f}</td></tr>' for r in records)
    sections=[]
    for r in records:
        n=r['image'][4:8];examples=', '.join(str(i) for i in r['example_b1_rows'])
        sections.append(f'''<section class="report-section image-case" id="image-{n}"><p class="eyebrow">IMG_{n} · 500 input corners</p><h2>From local structure<br>to 64 numbers.</h2><div class="example-layout"><figure class="location-map"><a href="figures/IMG_{n}_locations.jpg"><img src="figures/IMG_{n}_locations.jpg" alt="Six selected feature positions and 40-pixel support boxes in IMG {n}" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Six spatial examples. Orange support boxes surround the cyan corner centers. Labels show example number / B.1 row.</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="figures/IMG_{n}_examples.jpg"><img src="figures/IMG_{n}_examples.jpg" alt="Six feature examples each showing raw 40 by 40 region, blurred region, sampled 8 by 8 and normalized values" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Each example reads left to right: raw 40 × 40, blurred 40 × 40, sampled 8 × 8, normalized 8 × 8. Open the image to inspect the saved pixels and labels.</figcaption></figure></div><p>Zero-based B.1 rows shown: {examples}. Examples use six fixed spatial targets, not matches. All 500 input rows are retained; {r['valid_count']} descriptors are valid.</p><p>Maximum absolute normalized mean: {r['max_abs_valid_descriptor_mean']:.2g}; maximum std deviation from 1: {r['max_abs_valid_descriptor_std_error']:.2g}. Minimum sampled std is {r['std_min_in_bounds']:.5f}, above the 10⁻⁶ threshold.</p><p><a href="data/IMG_{n}.npz">Descriptors and all row data (NPZ)</a> · <a href="data/IMG_{n}.json">Row metadata (JSON)</a> · <a href="examples/IMG_{n}.npz">Six example arrays (NPZ)</a> · <a href="../B1/working/IMG_{n}.png">Unchanged B.1 working PNG</a> · <a href="../B1/report.html#image-{n}">B.1 corner selection</a></p></section>''')
    page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>B.2 · Describe the Patches</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../A3/page.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="page.css"></head><body class="report-page"><main class="shell">
<header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../index.html">Stitching Photo<br>Mosaics</a><nav class="header-nav" aria-label="B.2 navigation"><a href="../index.html">Project home <span>01</span></a><a href="#method">40 to 8 <span>02</span></a><a href="#results">Seven image results <span>03</span></a></nav></header>
<section class="project-hero"><p class="eyebrow">SYDE 671 · Assignment 3 · James Xie</p><h1>B.2 / DESCRIBE<br>THE PATCHES.</h1><p class="project-deck">Keep the local structure. Reduce the samples. Normalize the brightness.</p><div class="project-hero-rule"><span>Part B · Feature descriptors</span><span>3,500 features · 8 × 8 samples · 64 dimensions</span></div></section>
<section class="report-section"><h2>01 / A corner needs a description.</h2><figure class="result-figure"><a href="figures/IMG_8446_examples.jpg"><img src="figures/IMG_8446_examples.jpg" alt="Six local feature regions reduced from 40 by 40 to normalized 8 by 8 descriptors" loading="eager"></a><figcaption>Six examples from IMG_8446. Each raw region is summarized by 64 normalized values. The coordinate and B.1 candidate identity remain attached to every row.</figcaption></figure><p>B.2 uses seven 1200 × 1600 B.1 images and 500 corners each. Descriptors are axis aligned, without rotation alignment, a scale pyramid or Haar transform.</p></section>
<section class="report-section" id="method"><h2>02 / A large region, a small descriptor.</h2><p>Grayscale uses 0.299R + 0.587G + 0.114B on RGB/255. A 40 × 40 region uses symmetric offsets −19.5, −18.5, …, +19.5 around each corner (x, y).</p><p>Smooth the full image with Gaussian σ = 2, kernel 13 × 13 and REFLECT_101 boundaries. Handwritten bilinear sampling extracts raw and blurred 40 × 40 regions; patch edges are not reflected.</p><div class="formula">region offsets: −19.5, −18.5, …, +19.5
take region indices: 2, 7, 12, 17, 22, 27, 32, 37
8 × 8 sample offsets: −17.5, −12.5, …, +17.5</div><p>Sample every fifth element to obtain 8 × 8 values spanning the larger region. Smoothing reduces high frequencies and sensitivity to small shifts, without guaranteeing perfect anti-aliasing.</p><p>This follows the coarse-patch method in section 4 of <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2005/06/cvpr05.pdf">Brown, Szeliski &amp; Winder (2005)</a>. σ = 2 and sample-center conventions are implementation choices. OpenCV supplies Gaussian filtering only.</p></section>
<section class="report-section"><h2>03 / Remove bias and positive gain.</h2><div class="formula">v = flatten(sampled_8×8), in row-major order
μ = mean(v)       σ = population_std(v)
d = (v − μ) / σ</div><p>Valid descriptors have mean zero and population standard deviation one. This gives squared L2 norm about 64, rather than unit L2 norm.</p><p>Normalizing av + b removes positive gain and bias when values are unclipped. Negative gain flips the sign. Saturation, nonlinear lighting and reflections remain limitations; numerical values are not clipped.</p><p>Valid rows need full 40 × 40 support and standard deviation above 10⁻⁶. Invalid rows keep their IDs as zero vectors with a false flag and reason. B.3 excludes them.</p></section>
<section class="report-section" id="results"><h2>04 / Seven sets of 500 descriptors.</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Image</th><th>Input rows</th><th>Valid</th><th>Invalid</th><th>Minimum sampled std</th></tr></thead><tbody>''' + rows + '''</tbody></table></div><p>All 3,500 descriptors pass the same fixed threshold. Constant and border cases test invalid-row handling.</p><p>Raw, blurred and sampled tiles share [0, 1]. Normalized tiles use [−3, +3], with zero at middle gray. Only display values are clipped; numerical data is unchanged. Pixels are replicated for display.</p></section>''' + ''.join(sections) + '''
<section class="report-section"><h2>05 / Preserve identity for the next stage.</h2><p>Row i remains B.1 ANMS row i. Each record keeps its candidate ID, feature ID, coordinates and transform. No invalid row is dropped or reordered.</p><p>NPZ saves 500 × 64 float64 descriptors, 500 × 8 × 8 patches, statistics, validity, IDs, coordinates and transforms. JSON lists row metadata. Example arrays preserve each displayed sampling stage.</p><p>Hashes in <a href="measurements.json">measurements.json</a> verify unchanged inputs. These descriptors are not rotation or scale invariant; repeated windows can still look similar. Matching is shown in B.3.</p></section>
<section class="report-section"><h2>Reproduce &amp; inspect.</h2><pre>python run_descriptors.py
python build_report.py
python -m unittest test_descriptors -v</pre><p>Run from B2 in the existing NumPy/Pillow/OpenCV environment. No new dependency was installed.</p><p><a href="descriptors.py">Descriptor extraction and sampling</a> · <a href="run_descriptors.py">Real-image generation</a> · <a href="test_descriptors.py">Six analytical unit checks</a> · <a href="measurements.json">Parameters and dataset statistics</a> · <a href="../B1/report.html">B.1 corner locations</a></p><p>Checks cover exact ramp sampling, centered support, normalization, unclipped gain/bias changes and invalid inputs. All real descriptor rows and input hashes were verified.</p><p class="method-note">See B.3 for matches and B.4 for the automatic mosaic. The clarified requirement is one mosaic with at least three images.</p></section>
<nav class="project-home-nav" aria-label="Project navigation"><a class="solid-link" href="../index.html"><span aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span>Back to Project Home</a></nav>
<footer class="site-footer"><span>SYDE 671 · Assignment 3 · James Xie</span><span>B.2 · Axis-aligned patch descriptors</span></footer></main></body></html>'''
    (ROOT/'report.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
    (ROOT/'README.md').write_text('''# B.2 - Axis-aligned patch descriptors

Open report.html for the method, seven datasets and six spatial examples per photograph. B1 working PNGs and ANMS row identity are preserved. No descriptors are matched in this stage.

descriptors.py uses full-image Gaussian sigma2/kernel13/REFLECT_101, symmetric40x40 bilinear sample-center offsets-19.5..19.5, region indices2,7,...,37 to obtain8x8 (world offsets-17.5,-12.5,...17.5), then row-major flatten and population mean/std normalization. std must exceed1e-6; invalid rows retain zero vectors and false validity. Numerical values are never clipped. No rotation/scale normalization or Haar transform.

data/*.npz stores descriptors, sampled8, mean/std, flags, B1 rows/candidate indices, feature IDs, working/original coordinates and transforms. data/*.json stores row metadata/status. examples/*.npz preserves raw40/blur40/8x8/normalized arrays for six spatial examples. Figures use fixed display scales; normalized display clips to[-3,3] without clipping numerical data.

Run from B2:
```powershell
python run_descriptors.py
python build_report.py
python -m unittest test_descriptors -v
```

Six analytical unit checks passed. The current seven datasets each contain500 valid64D vectors. No new dependencies; upstream inputs are hash-checked unchanged. B3 matching and B4 automatic mosaicing remain upcoming.
''',encoding='utf-8')
    print('B2 report and README generated from seven saved datasets.')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
